{"questions":[{"questionNumber":1,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2023,"question":"<p>Given below are two statements:</p>\n<p>Statement I : High density polythene is formed in the presence of catalyst triethylaluminium and titanium tetrachloride.</p>\n<p>Statement II : High density polymers are chemically inert.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is false."},{"id":"B","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is true."},{"id":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true."},{"id":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false."}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"<p>NCERT Pg. 436 (Polymer)</p>"},{"questionNumber":2,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2023,"question":"<p>Which amongst the following molecules on polymerization produces neoprene?</p>","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://09639162073edf8505f7a384bd94de8a2efc507d86642fd29339df48e5f5fb11.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2023 Chemistry - Polymers Question 2 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"H\\(_2\\)C = CH \\(-\\) C \\(\\equiv\\) CH"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://988f12d0d182aecec301efc680b6b83997e45ded4d10daf4b19f19950523f192.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2023 Chemistry - Polymers Question 2 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"H\\(_2\\)C = CH \\(-\\) CH = CH\\(_2\\)"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://97c836a6873f6208c08394af8951a837db37a8418d35a07d121dd7f93b34f4e2.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2023 Chemistry - Polymers Question 2 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":3,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2022,"question":"<p>Which among the following is a thermoplastic polymer?</p>","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Melamine polymer"},{"id":"B","content":"Bakelite"},{"id":"C","content":"Polythene"},{"id":"D","content":"Urea-formaldehyde resin"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"<p>\\(\\bullet\\) Polythene is an example of thermoplastic polymer.</p>\n<p>Melamine polymer, Bakelite and Urea-formaldehyde resin are thermosetting polymers.</p>"},{"questionNumber":4,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2022,"question":"<p>Which statement regarding polymers is not correct?</p>","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Elastomers have polymer chains held together by weak intermolecular forces"},{"id":"B","content":"Fibers possess high tensile strength"},{"id":"C","content":"Thermoplastic polymers are capable of repeatedly softening and hardening on heating and cooling respectively"},{"id":"D","content":"Thermosetting polymers are reusable"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"<p>\\(\\bullet\\) Thermoplastic polymers are the linear or slightly long chain molecules capable of repeatedly softening and hardening on cooling.</p>\n<p>\\(\\bullet\\) Thermosetting polymers are cross-linked or heavily branched molecules, which on heating undergo extensive cross-linking in moulds and again become infusible. These cannot be reused.</p>\n<p>\\(\\bullet\\) Elastomers have polymer chains held together by weak intermolecular forces.</p>\n<p>\\(\\bullet\\) Fibres possess high tensile strength.</p>"},{"questionNumber":5,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2021,"question":"Which one of the following polymers is prepared by addition polymerisation?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Dacron"},{"id":"B","content":"Teflon"},{"id":"C","content":"Nylon-66"},{"id":"D","content":"Novolac"}],"correctOption":"B","solution":"","explanation":"Dacron, Nylon-66 and Novolac are prepared by condensation polymerisation.<br><br>Teflon is an addition polymer. Monomer of teflon is tetrafluoroethene.<br><br><img src=\"pyq-asset://8aba89cd61d0f9df7e8b955f0e0e0b78e3b28ce6526367ea77eb0c7c886bcfe8.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2021 Chemistry - Polymers Question 5 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":6,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2021,"question":"The reagent 'R' in the given sequence of chemical reaction is :<br><br><img src=\"pyq-asset://51bfebcdc5885cb2db982d628ee8887ac3f5c844572d99c1f0459f9fd992eb72.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2021 Chemistry - Polymers Question 6 English\">","options":[{"id":"A","content":"CuCN/KCN"},{"id":"B","content":"H<sub>2</sub>O"},{"id":"C","content":"CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>OH"},{"id":"D","content":"HI"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://143c7824c27dd9f2710e3a6fb7b20631cf84cbbe1a63afe1181b815d433824b8.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2021 Chemistry - Polymers Question 6 English Explanation\"><br>Reagent R is C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>5</sub>OH with diazonium salt."},{"questionNumber":7,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2020,"question":"Which of the following is a natural polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"poly (Butadiene-styrene)"},{"id":"B","content":"polybutadiene"},{"id":"C","content":"poly (Butadiene-acrylonitrile)"},{"id":"D","content":"cis-1, 4-polyisoprene"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Naturally occurring polymer, natural rubber is cis-1, 4-polyisoprene."},{"questionNumber":8,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2019,"question":"The biodegradable polymer is :","options":[{"id":"A","content":"nylon-6"},{"id":"B","content":"Buna-S"},{"id":"C","content":"nylon-6, 6"},{"id":"D","content":"nylon-2-nylon 6"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Biodegradable polymer is Nylon-2-Nylon-6."},{"questionNumber":9,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2018,"question":"Regarding cross-linked or network polymers,\nwhich of the following statements is incorrect?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"They contain covalent bonds between\nvarious linear polymer chains."},{"id":"B","content":"They are formed from bi- and tri-functional\nmonomers."},{"id":"C","content":"Examples are bakelite and melamine."},{"id":"D","content":"They contain strong covalent bonds in\ntheir polymer chains."}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Cross-linked or network polymers are usually\nformed from bi-functional &amp; tri-functional\nmonomers and contains strong covalent bond\nbetween various linear polymer chains like\nMelamine, Bakelite etc."},{"questionNumber":10,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2016,"question":"Which one of the following structures represents nylon 6, 6 polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://64157efbc7146d3e06c1e7edc4a12c1583977f976bf92103b846b83a1c98774c.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 2 Chemistry - Polymers Question 12 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://878bf90c1fa6c340905649acd248330dbe47a7e5095e7ef5de6ae7fb4a0523ff.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 2 Chemistry - Polymers Question 12 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://b63f99ec3c7678fea1ab0e67932ba20c842c367abd4926838eb1307b09bf2eff.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 2 Chemistry - Polymers Question 12 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://ccefa37d7977075d03c3f58850a8535f8cd8c9a0243ea6534b562bc4382b6ed9.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 2 Chemistry - Polymers Question 12 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://ca7651d386dbe740d7e93a73042dcbcaac868443790f89fab4ea342f13210873.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 2 Chemistry - Polymers Question 12 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":11,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2016,"question":"Natural rubber has","options":[{"id":"A","content":"alternate <i>cis</i>- and <i>trans</i>-configuration"},{"id":"B","content":"random <i>cis</i>- and <i>trans</i>-configuration"},{"id":"C","content":"all <i>cis</i>-configuration"},{"id":"D","content":"all <i>trans</i>-configuration."}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"Natural rubber is cis-polyisoprene.\n<img src=\"pyq-asset://e1af9fc1464a66720d1bd91d9f52528d9b6f714d021aa6891802f752615011ba.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2016 Phase 1 Chemistry - Polymers Question 35 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":12,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2015,"question":"Caprolactam is used for the manufacture of","options":[{"id":"A","content":"teflon"},{"id":"B","content":"terylene"},{"id":"C","content":"nylon 6, 6"},{"id":"D","content":"nylon 6."}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://232fb37e80c88339e5066e03c62e07290a0da0594e8c8e9c8bb5a5ad3a4d077a.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2015 Chemistry - Polymers Question 34 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":13,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2015,"question":"Biodegradable polymer which can be produced from glycine and aminocaproic acid is","options":[{"id":"A","content":"buna - N"},{"id":"B","content":"nylon 6, 6"},{"id":"C","content":"nylon 2-nylon 6"},{"id":"D","content":"PHBV"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://44a64c2984e5ff64d2d13ca9e74075d9a0a2a33357a6037bd86b01fc4dc3e09b.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2015 Cancelled Paper Chemistry - Polymers Question 33 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":14,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2014,"question":"Which of the following organic compounds polymerizes to form the polyester dacron?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Propylene and <i>para</i> HO\\(-\\)(C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>)\\(-\\)OH"},{"id":"B","content":"Benzoic acid and ethanol"},{"id":"C","content":"Terephthalic acid and ethylene glycol"},{"id":"D","content":"Benzoic acid and <i>para</i> HO\\(-\\)(C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>)\\(-\\)OH"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://09b1730e30564913b2f3057a70b74999ca4974f7eedce42675a1b9a187a8cf97.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2014 Chemistry - Polymers Question 32 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":15,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2014,"question":"Which one of the following is an example of thermosetting polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://9d8dfd79b5c0290a056690075dd6c51a634286060f0fca66c07844ea8b554d22.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2014 Chemistry - Polymers Question 11 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://7797c07d199f187ace04451c6e565e1ec243e2724802615f507a119d42a333a1.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2014 Chemistry - Polymers Question 11 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://01ba0841e9c090ab952def168299aaa7231476d7ac043ee11a263cb51f7c27a7.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2014 Chemistry - Polymers Question 11 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://5c0f0757f0740f511be9133d5c04bd6e42a95f03fa352a04c5dc2c5ca8c13d76.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2014 Chemistry - Polymers Question 11 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Thermosetting polymers undergo chemical changes when heated and set to hard mass when cooled e.g. Bakelite."},{"questionNumber":16,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2013,"question":"Nylon is an example of","options":[{"id":"A","content":"polyamide"},{"id":"B","content":"polythene"},{"id":"C","content":"polyester"},{"id":"D","content":"polysaccharide."}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Nylon is a polyamide."},{"questionNumber":17,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2013,"question":"Which is the monomer of neoprene in the following?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://8f0e78c3a0cbf3db7b38c440ab4f18fa39cd98b43d60c59919fd030e8c63fcd5.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2013 Chemistry - Polymers Question 13 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://3f2e7a4f17f4bf1a0d86f25eeb85fd8c026eb9fd4dc7bc33a8edb450819a9466.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2013 Chemistry - Polymers Question 13 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://3b54169e2d91263a3babaa7f95dd74a3cc3a226d79d65b0f10c07928c1360a0b.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2013 Chemistry - Polymers Question 13 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://8124bd0272a8fe3a55514e99ce971abc41967f7489ccc76c888b51bd0e992c92.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2013 Chemistry - Polymers Question 13 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Chloroprene is the monomer of neoprene.\n<br><br><img src=\"pyq-asset://cb7a71b0cd66c36cc092bc6a5287fe5c0f2a8984fa410e4f228b3b2f49275ea8.webp\" alt=\"NEET 2013 Chemistry - Polymers Question 13 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":18,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2012,"question":"Which one of the following sets forms the biodegradable polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://022a1722ae7b2cf6e99e69c24675b8c54c2e8ba8da69d0f0211a884e2b3bf33a.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2012 Mains Chemistry - Polymers Question 14 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://be3b1f385719f0081257922796cb7e0e9e999c481d895541a13e190086712e0b.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2012 Mains Chemistry - Polymers Question 14 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://aaebc0c98345f91895af046e035b1f44d8e251695e053a74b8c71b66e18a4bbb.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2012 Mains Chemistry - Polymers Question 14 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://fbd06b3e7d044f950736b6cb3c0039d4cd0635ca748632f20c25e77929427b73.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2012 Mains Chemistry - Polymers Question 14 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"B","solution":"","explanation":"Biodegradable polymer is Nylon-2-Nylon-6 which is copolymer of glycine (H<sub>2</sub>N – CH<sub>2</sub>– COOH) and amino caproic acid (H<sub>2</sub>N–(CH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>5</sub> – COOH)."},{"questionNumber":19,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2012,"question":"Which of the following statements is false?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Artificial silk is derived from cellulose."},{"id":"B","content":"Nylon-6, 6 is an example of elastomer."},{"id":"C","content":"The repeat unit in natural rubber is isoprene."},{"id":"D","content":"Both starch and cellulose are polymers of glucose."}],"correctOption":"B","solution":"","explanation":"Nylon 6, 6 is an example of fibers."},{"questionNumber":20,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2012,"question":"Which one of the following is not a condensation polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Melamine"},{"id":"B","content":"Glyptal"},{"id":"C","content":"Dacron"},{"id":"D","content":"Neoprene"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"<p>Neoprene is made by joining smaller molecules together without losing any atoms. This process is called addition polymerization.</p>\n<p>Condensation polymers are made when small molecules, like water, are released during the reaction. Neoprene does not form this way.</p>\n<p>So, Neoprene is not a condensation polymer.</p>"},{"questionNumber":21,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2011,"question":"Of the following which one is classified as polyester polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Terylene"},{"id":"B","content":"Bakelite"},{"id":"C","content":"Melamine"},{"id":"D","content":"Nylon-6,6"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Terylene (Dacron) is a polyester polymer."},{"questionNumber":22,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2010,"question":"Which of the following structures represents neoprene polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://3486db99e10b3c5690501e49cd0de9258c8d587c4493b57df579f373da7f01d6.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2010 Prelims Chemistry - Polymers Question 15 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://120dbf284ffa0095ba4a18e3e702033fcb143ea30fdf1007e14b691d7addd752.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2010 Prelims Chemistry - Polymers Question 15 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://cc2db7f020c714122aed9a9a5a0ad4e4c9e8bcad0e2e68a869b0484e168c145e.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2010 Prelims Chemistry - Polymers Question 15 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://334e756bc108f037924ed2beec5c8038c0e642ebe8ca253b0af07f810d05b6ab.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2010 Prelims Chemistry - Polymers Question 15 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Neoprene is :\n<br><img src=\"pyq-asset://3486db99e10b3c5690501e49cd0de9258c8d587c4493b57df579f373da7f01d6.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2010 Prelims Chemistry - Polymers Question 15 English Explanation\">\n<br><br>It is a polymer of chloroprene."},{"questionNumber":23,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2009,"question":"Structures of some common polymers are given. Which one is not correctly presented?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://8428902db78bf31a49a169c8ec2abb9eac50a9f1c1083f2acadf99c6f883b89e.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2009 Chemistry - Polymers Question 16 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://96a0b9c0942189dede2b0c84038ea094ef0bd4365f3bd171b3292938a752ccb4.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2009 Chemistry - Polymers Question 16 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://458aecec534ca7fef3cb73af20bf5ff03e6c341cc18492fe62227fee9cb12908.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2009 Chemistry - Polymers Question 16 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://c612fbad3613aff578e6f5b763398f5740a2965a6e6f7b09f16ae254fb24daea.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2009 Chemistry - Polymers Question 16 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"The structure of neoprene is\n<br><img src=\"pyq-asset://31cb0fcaa0d0634f1e62584851cb8aac5fa6f82a5ba7768082667f4c9ee6b548.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2009 Chemistry - Polymers Question 16 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":24,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2008,"question":"Which one of the following statements is not true?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Buna-S is a copolymer of butadiene and styrene."},{"id":"B","content":"Natural rubber is a, 1,4-polymer of isoprene."},{"id":"C","content":"In vulcanization, the formation of sulphur bridges between different chains make rubber harder and stronger."},{"id":"D","content":"Natural rubber has the <i>trans</i>-configuration at every double bond."}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Natural rubber is cis-1, 3 polyisoprene and has only cis-configuration about the double bond."},{"questionNumber":25,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2007,"question":"Which  one of the following polymers is prepared by condensation polymerisation?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Teflon"},{"id":"B","content":"Natural rubber"},{"id":"C","content":"Styrene"},{"id":"D","content":"Nylon-6,6"}],"correctOption":"D","solution":"","explanation":"Nylon-6,6 is a condensation polymer of adipic acid and hexamethylene diamine.\n<img src=\"pyq-asset://f2b71c089de53d2934e69c3e7b36b0e88502035fa676cd0b3c790a69215fc160.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2007 Chemistry - Polymers Question 26 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":26,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2006,"question":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://1550cfa85b77311eb9a59b2d3ced2822e7b43105330f55ba6933f42b0505c96c.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2006 Chemistry - Polymers Question 10 English\">\n<br>is a","options":[{"id":"A","content":"homopolymer"},{"id":"B","content":"copolymer"},{"id":"C","content":"addition polymer"},{"id":"D","content":"thermosetting polymer."}],"correctOption":"B","solution":"","explanation":"It is formed by the condensation of adipic acid and hexamethylene diamine. It is a copolymer."},{"questionNumber":27,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2005,"question":"The monomer of the polymer\n<br><img src=\"pyq-asset://1cf363f4ab9f2612f6320123d5dcde37493c0752fd2b33074d31e3280aba55d8.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2005 Chemistry - Polymers Question 17 English\">","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://8e6044a1965ae1d3ee5003c0c56ec7d8e6ecac91fa0fa6ff8479141bd7203f82.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2005 Chemistry - Polymers Question 17 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"CH<sub>3</sub>CH\\(=\\)CHCH<sub>3</sub>"},{"id":"C","content":"CH<sub>3</sub>CH\\(=\\)CH<sub>2</sub>"},{"id":"D","content":"(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>C\\(=\\)C(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://fa4d1cdb2981e8d14fa50eb195d3f54f593f744ef12316925fdea498d2985f76.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2005 Chemistry - Polymers Question 17 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":28,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2004,"question":"Which one of the following is a chain growth polymer?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"Starch"},{"id":"B","content":"Nucleic acid"},{"id":"C","content":"Polystyrene"},{"id":"D","content":"Protein"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"Polystyrene is a chain growth polymer.\n<img src=\"pyq-asset://3ded88f596a1706ce12f29a2300c23f0c16a9f6dd13132f7f8b88a415c79eccd.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2004 Chemistry - Polymers Question 25 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":29,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2003,"question":"Which one of the following monomers gives the polymer neoprene on polymerization?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"CH<sub>2</sub>\\(=\\)CHCl"},{"id":"B","content":"CCl<sub>2</sub>\\(=\\)CCl<sub>2</sub>"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://9ac4a56e267d8c7ac329e6f63983410c04019254c265614052a1d9cede58111f.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 20 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"CF<sub>2</sub>\\(=\\)CF<sub>2</sub>"}],"correctOption":"C","solution":"","explanation":"Chloroprene (2-chloro-1, 3-butadiene) on addition polymerisation gives neoprene."},{"questionNumber":30,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2003,"question":"Acrilan is a hard, horny and a high melting material. Which one of the following represents its structure?","options":[{"id":"A","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://fc6f014491508675e070dc552940d6513e4edfb81f172f9c14dd35ef02c503e1.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 21 English Option 1\">"},{"id":"B","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://2c366fab8a5b6e9eae49eb37d93cceea9fc412186e39b10426fe93ad21c76f3f.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 21 English Option 2\">"},{"id":"C","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://148cf4befc83f7968325eeecca4ab4d8db72fb74d37755b89402c48a589645d5.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 21 English Option 3\">"},{"id":"D","content":"<img src=\"pyq-asset://03e0050f7e634832a8a8d1fa570de8799adc481846447aad1705e2b2ce1194f6.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 21 English Option 4\">"}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Acrilan is an addition polymer of acrylonitrile.\n<img src=\"pyq-asset://d259e2708e8f17a071c8e32ccacc687578988f2229b18a27146490c10a191723.webp\" alt=\"AIPMT 2003 Chemistry - Polymers Question 21 English Explanation\">"},{"questionNumber":31,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-polymers","year":2002,"question":"Cellulose is polymer of","options":[{"id":"A","content":"glucose"},{"id":"B","content":"fructose"},{"id":"C","content":"ribose"},{"id":"D","content":"sucrose."}],"correctOption":"A","solution":"","explanation":"Cellulose is a straight chain polysaccharide composed of D-glucose units joined by \\(\\beta\\)-glycosidic linkage."},{"questionNumber":32,"topic":"classification-preparations-and-properties-of-pol